{#
    One navigation item for the application shell (designs/event_builder.svg).

    Lives in its own file rather than as a `{% macro %}` inside the layout because a macro
    declared in a template that `extends` another is only reliably reachable through an explicit
    import, and a shell that silently rendered no navigation would be a very quiet bug.

    `current` is passed in rather than compared here: which route counts as "this section" is a
    question about the section, not about the item, and a coach's My Times and a player's Best
    Times answer it differently.
#}
{% import '_icons.html.twig' as icons %}

{% macro item(url, label, iconName, current) %}
    {% import '_icons.html.twig' as icons %}
    <li>
        {#
            `aria-current="page"` is the state; the CSS keys off the attribute so the highlighted
            item and the announced item are always the same item. The bold weight and the border
            carry it as well as the tint, because colour alone is not a cue (WCAG 1.4.1).
        #}
        <a class="pp-nav-item" href="{{ url }}"{% if current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
            {{ icons.icon(iconName) }}
            <span>{{ label }}</span>
        </a>
    </li>
{% endmacro %}
